  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0">Context + rigor declaration per task-execute Step 0.5. Read pcf-build-scaffold.md, R1 lessons-learned.md, and the recorded task-001 spike outcome. If the spike outcome is missing or contradicts the manifest plan, STOP (escalation trigger 1).</step>
    <step order="1">Scaffold src/client/pcf/RecordHeader/ by copying the MatterHeader folder structure (control/, Solution/, __tests__/, package.json, tsconfig.json, featureconfig.json, webpack.config.js, jest configs); rename all identity strings to Spaarke.Records.RecordHeader / RecordHeaderPcf; set version 1.1.0 everywhere it appears.</step>
    <step order="2">Author control/ControlManifest.Input.xml: boundField/title/showVersion carried over, layoutJson added with the spike-decided of-type; verify by grep that no manifest attribute value contains an apostrophe.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify package.json: prebuild + prebuild:prod ensure-dist-fresh lines, build:prod with --buildMode production, ajv ^8.12.0 devDependency.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement control/index.ts: standard virtual-control lifecycle; FR-12 self-detection (contextInfo primary, context.page fallback, type-cast idiom); pass entityName, recordId, title, showVersion, and the raw layoutJson string to the host.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement control/RecordHeaderHost.tsx: FluentProvider wrap mirroring MatterHeaderHost (incl. theme handling), rendering RecordHeaderView.</step>
    <step order="6">Implement control/RecordHeaderView.tsx: build the resolver's metadata input from the form/metadata surface established by Phase 2 (per the 022 hook contract), call resolveHeaderConfig, render RecordHeaderShell (columns from resolved config) + FieldGrid + per-renderer cells (text/textarea/date/number/boolean/optionset via the fields barrel; lookup via the 023 cell), toolbar via useRecordHeaderToolbarActions, version footer from version.ts. All shared-lib imports deep-path dist/*.</step>
    <step order="7">Delete the stale exports-map comment at MatterHeaderView.tsx lines 53-62 (no other MatterHeader change).</step>
    <step order="8">Author Solution/: solution.xml (UniqueName RecordHeaderPcf, RootComponent type 66), customizations.xml, [Content_Types].xml, pack.ps1; confirm the 5-location version sync (1.1.0).</step>
    <step order="9">Write/adapt __tests__/RecordHeaderView.test.tsx from the MatterHeader test as a config-driven suite (valid layoutJson, absent layoutJson, malformed layoutJson paths).</step>
    <step order="10">Run npm run build:prod; record the bundle byte size in notes and verify at or under 250 KB; run npm test; both green.</step>
    <step order="11">Pack the solution ZIP via pack.ps1 and import into spaarkedev1 via the pcf-deploy skill; verify with pac solution list. Bind the control on a dev/test form for verification ONLY — the six production main-form bindings are Phase 5 (tasks 050-080).</step>
    <step order="12">Execute the ui-tests below (task-execute Step 9.7); record results.</step>
    <step order="13">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="14">Document deviations + the confirmed starting version + bundle/TTI measurements in projects/record-header-and-notepad-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the task-001 spike outcome contradicts the manifest plan — the recorded of-type decision is missing, or the spike found that NEITHER of-type Multiple NOR SingleLine.Text presents a usable editor / survives an export-import round-trip — STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md section 6. Do NOT invent a third configuration mechanism (config table, bound column, web resource).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the hoisted machinery contracts from tasks 022/023 do not expose what the generic view needs (e.g. the hook cannot stage a renderer's value type, or the lookup cell cannot take metadata-resolved targets), STOP and escalate rather than re-implementing save/search machinery in the PCF layer — forking shared primitives is a spec MUST NOT.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>src/client/pcf/MatterHeader/ — the shipped v1.0.20 per-entity control this task generalizes (grep: the only RecordHeader-composition PCF in src/client/pcf/).</existing>
    <extension>This IS the extension: the same control generalized under a clean identity, with the old one retired at task 081. Owner decision B (reaffirmed 2026-08-22) chose new-identity + one-time Matter re-bind over renaming in place; a pure in-place extension would freeze the Matter-flavoured schema name into every future entity's form XML.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the configurable control, the withdrawn plan returns: four more per-entity PCF solutions to version, deploy, bind and fix in parallel, with ~82 lines of form-buffer/lookup machinery duplicated 4x (spec section 11), and every future entity needs a code change + build + new solution instead of a form edit. The field payload stays compiled in (FR-01 cost).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Derived defaults render (no layoutJson)">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn={test-entity}&amp;id={record-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Open a record of the dev-bound test entity with the layoutJson property left blank</step>
        <step>Verify the header renders: primary name field first (span 2) plus up to 4 further fields, toolbar with title, version footer v1.1.0</step>
        <step>Check the console for JavaScript errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Control renders tier-2 derived defaults with zero console errors — never blank</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Configured layout renders (valid layoutJson)">
      <steps>
        <step>In the form designer, paste a valid v1.0 layout (title, columns, 4+ fields with spans) into layoutJson; save + publish</step>
        <step>Reload the record; verify fields, order, spans, and title match the pasted config</step>
        <step>Verify the loading skeleton shown before data resolves matches the configured column count (no 3-column flash for a columns 2 layout)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Rendered layout matches the configuration exactly, including skeleton column parity</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Malformed layoutJson degrades (FR-03/NFR-10)">
      <steps>
        <step>Set layoutJson to {{{ ; save + publish; reload the record</step>
        <step>Verify the header renders derived defaults and one console.warn appears (no thrown error, no blank section)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>console.warn + derived defaults; the form is never blanked</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Form-buffer edit stages without re-render flash (FR-13)">
      <steps>
        <step>Edit a text field inline and commit with Enter</step>
        <step>Verify the form's Save button activates (dirty) and the header does NOT flash its loading skeleton</step>
        <step>Save the form; verify the value persists</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Edit stages to the form buffer; no PCF re-render flash; form Save commits</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Missing-field config fails loudly (FR-14)">
      <steps>
        <step>Configure layoutJson naming a field that exists on the entity but is NOT on the form; reload</step>
        <step>Attempt an inline edit on that cell</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The edit surfaces the loud thrown error (Field not on form); the input is never silently dropped</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode in model-driven app settings and reload</step>
        <step>Verify card background, text, skeleton, and the sparkle/To Do/Notepad popover surfaces adapt (no white-on-dark blocks, no black-on-light text)</step>
        <step>Verify portal-rendered popovers have proper chrome (background, shadow, radius) — the FluentProvider wrap is working</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All colors resolve from Fluent v9 semantic tokens in both themes, including portal surfaces</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Build PCF (npm run build:prod — NEVER npm run build for deployable bundles) and run tests</tool>
    <tool name="pac">Solution pack/import/list via the pcf-deploy skill</tool>
