  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">npm run build:prod exits 0; bundle.js is at or under 250 KB minified; the measured byte size and the diff vs the R1 62.4 KiB baseline are recorded in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep of ControlManifest.Input.xml and Solution/Controls/sprk_Spaarke.Records.RecordHeader/ControlManifest.xml finds ZERO apostrophes inside attribute values.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">package.json contains prebuild AND prebuild:prod ensure-dist-fresh entries and a build:prod script invoking pcf-scripts build --buildMode production; ajv ^8.12.0 is a devDependency.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep of src/client/pcf/RecordHeader/ shows every @spaarke/ui-components import uses a dist/* deep path and no direct @fluentui/react-icons import exists in the PCF layer.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: grep of src/client/pcf/RecordHeader/control/ finds no compiled-in entity logical name (no sprk_matter, sprk_project, etc.) and no literal record GUID or environment name.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">control/index.ts reads entityTypeName/entityId from context.mode.contextInfo with a context.page fallback, both via the type-cast idiom.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The manifest carries boundField (bound, required), title, showVersion, and layoutJson (usage input) whose of-type matches the recorded task-001 spike outcome.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Version 1.1.0 is present and identical in all FIVE locations (ControlManifest.Input.xml, version.ts, solution.xml, Solution ControlManifest.xml, pack.ps1) and renders in the footer.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The solution ZIP packs via pack.ps1 and imports into spaarkedev1; pac solution list shows RecordHeaderPcf; the control appears in the form-designer gallery.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RecordHeaderView.tsx contains no direct Xrm.Page attribute access and no OData search-builder code — machinery only via the 022 hook and 023 cell (code inspection at review).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MatterHeaderView.tsx lines 53-62 stale exports-map comment is deleted with no functional MatterHeader change, and no equivalent comment exists in RecordHeaderView.tsx.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Unit tests pass (valid/absent/malformed layoutJson paths) and all six ui-tests above executed with results recorded.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    STATUS 2026-08-25 — steps 0-10 COMPLETE and green; steps 11-12 BLOCKED on an NFR-02
    escalation. Full record: notes/decisions/033-recordheader-pcf-bundle-nfr02.md

    Build green, 35/35 PCF tests, 473/473 shared-lib tests, lint green, ZIP packs, version
    1.1.0 synced across all 5 locations, zero apostrophes in both manifests.

    BLOCKER: bundle.js is 377,680 bytes vs the 250 KB NFR-02 ceiling (+51%). Measured
    attribution: @fluentui/react-datepicker-compat (reached via DateField, required by FR-06)
    costs 284,974 B = 75% of the bundle; everything else is 92,706 B, well inside budget. The
    *-compat packages sit outside the platform-library Fluent externalization. The fallback
    documented in wave1-sideeffects-tree-shaking.md (lazy deep-path DateField import) was
    TESTED and does NOT work: pcf-scripts emits a single chunk, so React.lazy inlines straight
    back and the bundle grows 1,415 B. Solution packed but deliberately NOT imported to
    spaarkedev1; ui-tests need the deployed control. Owner decision required between raising
    the ceiling (recommended - 250 KB predates FR-06) and replacing DatePicker in task 010.

    Shared-lib extension made under CLAUDE.md section 11: useRecordHeaderFields gained
    saveValue/displayValue because task 022 staged text+lookup only while FR-06/07/08/09 need
    Date/number/boolean staging. Put in the shared hook, NOT forked into the PCF layer.

    New build gotcha for pcf-build-scaffold.md (recommend adding as #11): the manifest entry
    module must define EXACTLY ONE export - a second one fails with pcf-1023.

    Findings requested: ZERO polymorphic lookups across the six rollout layouts (all 7 lookups
    single-target), so 023 targets[0] is sufficient. String+TextArea deriving 'text' does NOT
    bite - every multiline field in every layout is Memo, which derives 'textarea' correctly.

    Spec refs: FR-01, FR-12, NFR-01/02/08/09/11; design 5.1-5.4, 6.3. TTI budget (NFR-01: 300 ms
